{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 42,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, Maschil, for the sons of Korah. As the hart panteth after the water brooks, so my soul panteth after thee, O God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My soul thirsteth for God, for the living God: when shall I come and appear before God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My tears have been my food day and night, while they continually say to me, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I remember these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I pour out my soul in me: for I had gone with the multitude, I went with them to the house of God, with the voice of joy and praise, with a multitude that kept holy-day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "why",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " art thou disquieted in me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the help of his countenance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my God, my soul is cast down within me: therefore will I remember thee from the land of Jordan, and of the Hermonites, from the hill Mizar.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Deep calleth to deep at the noise of thy water-spouts: all thy waves and thy billows are gone over me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD will command his loving-kindness in the day-time, and in the night his song ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my prayer to the God of my life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will say to God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me? why go I mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with a sword in my bones, my enemies reproach me; while they say daily to me, Where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.42.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.42.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the health of my countenance, and my God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
